Subject: [PATCH 055/220] [ae-patch] Lay the Agents pane out like Claude
 Desktop's Background tasks and draw its graph left to right.

The right pane is usually taller than wide, so the top-down agent tree came
out about 2000 px wide and fitView shrank it to unreadable dots. The graph
now lays out left to right when the pane is taller than wide (with a
per-device auto / top-down / left-right toggle) and stops at a readable
zoom, anchored on the root, so the pane pans instead of shrinking. It
refits only when the node set, direction or pane size changes, so a poll
leaves the user's pan and zoom alone.

The list now shows Running agents (working, awaiting input or launching)
first with a live timer, the routed model and the last line ("No output
yet" until there is one), folds everything else into one counted Finished
line with a per-session Clear, and puts the open chat's task list (Claude
Code's TodoWrite items) in a folding Plan section below. A Stop square
appears only on agents OmniGent launched: Claude Code's own subagents run
inside the main agent's process, so an interrupt to their mirror does
nothing. The child-session hook now keeps created_at and updated_at, which
the server already sent, for the timers.
